      "problem": "Solve the absolute value inequality $|3x+2|<7.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x<$\n{{field-3}}",
      "worked_solution": "We convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $3x+2$ whose distance from zero is less than $7.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-7<3x+2<7\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7<3x+2 & <7 \\\\ -9<3x & <5 \\\\ -3<x & <\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
